  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IGAD REGIONAL REFUGEE MANAGEMENT PHASE  II - IGAD REGIONAL REFUGEE MANAGEMENT PHASE II</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">IGAD REGIONAL REFUGEE MANAGEMENT PHASE II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xF6;det f&#xF6;r IGAD:s andra fas kommer att bygga p&#xE5; de framsteg som gjorts i den f&#xF6;rsta fasen, s&#xE4;rskilt vad g&#xE4;ller utvecklingen, valideringen och godk&#xE4;nnandet av IGAD:s policyramverk f&#xF6;r flyktingskydd. Den andra fasens st&#xF6;d kommer att fokusera p&#xE5; genomf&#xF6;randet av policyramverket med ett djupare samarbete med flyktingar, flyktingledda och kvinnoledda organisationer. Programmet kommer att tillhandah&#xE5;lla tekniskt st&#xF6;d till medlemsstaterna i syfte att anpassa och harmonisera nationella strategier med det regionala policyramverket, samt st&#xE4;rka skyddsresponsen f&#xF6;r flyktingar i regionen. Dessutom kommer programmet att st&#xE4;rka IGAD-medlemsstaternas kapacitet i processer f&#xF6;r fastst&#xE4;llande av flyktingstatus samt &#xF6;ka effektiviteten i dessa processer. &apos;Gender Equality&apos; &#xE4;r markerat som ett viktigt m&#xE5;l f&#xF6;r detta program, eftersom programmet kommer att genomf&#xF6;ra en genusanalys och erbjuda utbildning till medlemsstaterna vad g&#xE4;ller olika genusaspekter i policyutveckling samt tillhandah&#xE5;lla tekniskt st&#xF6;d f&#xF6;r att integrera genusk&#xE4;nsliga element i flyktinghanteringspolicyers och strategier. Dessutom syftar programmet till att &#xF6;ka kvinnors och kvinnoledda organisationers deltagande i diskussioner om policyf&#xF6;r&#xE4;ndringar med beslutsfattare p&#xE5; nationell och subnationell niv&#xE5;.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The IGAD second phase support will build on the progress made in the first phase support, specifically the development, validation, and endorsement of the IGAD Policy Framework on Refugee Protection. The second phase support will focus on the implementation of the policy framework with more engagement of refugees, refugee-led and women-led organizations.  The program will provide technical assistance to MS to align national policies to the regional Policy framework, facilitating the harmonization of policies in the region as well as improving the refugee protection space in the region. Moreover, the program will strengthen the capacity of IGAD Member States in Refugee Status Determination (RSD) processes and aim to increase efficiency in these processes.

The program has marked &apos;Gender Equality&apos; as a significant objective as the program will conduct a gender analysis, and provide technical assistance to Member States to revise national refugee management policies with gender considerations.

Furthermore, the program aims to enhance the participation of women and women-led organizations in policy change discussions with policy makers.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The interventions has the following specific objectives:

i. Enhance access to fundamental rights and freedoms for refugees and asylum seekers in line with the principle of age, gender and diversity and promote a harmonized, conducive policy environment to maintain the asylum space in the Member States;
ii. Promote localized approaches, establish effective people-centered and gender-responsive approaches to address forced displacement in the IGAD region;
iii. Strengthen the institutional capacities of Member States to effectively implement the IGAD Policy Framework on Refugee Protection, and related regional frameworks and mechanisms that promote the protection and management of forcibly displaced persons in the region;
iv. Strengthen the Durable Solutions initiatives in the IGAD region to address displacement at national and subnational levels; and
v. Enhance Project Management and Institutional Capacity.</narrative>
  </description>
